= Opening sequence

EXT. CITY ROOFTOP - NIGHT

Wind howls across the rooftop. A figure crouches at the edge, watching the street below.

INT. SURVEILLANCE VAN - CONTINUOUS

MARCUS adjusts a dial. Static fills the speakers.

MARCUS
(into radio)
Tell me you see her.

KAI (V.O.)
She's moving. *Fast.*

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. ARCHIVE VAULT - NIGHT

Rain slams against the tempered glass skylight. Water cascades down the reinforced concrete buttresses.

ELENA (30s), wrapped in a soaked ballistic duster, shoves the rusted hydraulic lever downward. Gears groan with forty years of silence.

ELENA
(into comm-link, strained)
The primary locking pins didn't drop. Tell me you have the secondary frequency, Marcus.

MARCUS (O.S.)
Static on this end. The storm's scrambling the satellite tether. You have forty-five seconds before local security cycles the grid.

ELENA
Then start counting.

CLOSE ON ELENA'S HANDS

She wedges a titanium pry bar between the split casing. A violet spark leaps out, reflecting across her visor.

> THE END <
